<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khaleda Zia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khaleda Zia, the widow of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziaur-rahman">Ziaur Rahman</a>, became leader of the Bangladesh Nationalist Party in 1984 and joined the movement that ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussain-muhammad-ershad">Hussain Muhammad Ershad</a>'s rule in 1990. She was Bangladesh's first woman prime minister, serving from 1991 to 1996 and from 2001 to 2006, and her long rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-hasina">Sheikh Hasina</a> dominated national politics. She was imprisoned on corruption charges in 2018 and fully freed in 2024.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khaleda-zia.jpg" alt="Khaleda Zia" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Department of State from United States · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khaleda_Zia_Poses_for_a_Photo_with_Secretary_Kerry_at_U.S._Embassy_Dhaka_(29284522026)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
